===Tone===
Bangolan has [[Tone (linguistics)#Lexical tones and grammatical tones|lexical and grammatical tone]]. Lexical tone contrasts {{IPA|bgj|nd͡zɔ̂ŋ||}} {{gloss|clitoris}} with {{IPA|bgj|nd͡zɔ̏ŋ||}} {{gloss|thorn}},{{sfn|Njeck|2003a|p=14}} while grammatical tone contrasts {{IPA|bgj|à wé||}} {{gloss|he has gone}} with {{IPA|bgj|à wē||}} {{gloss|he is going}}.{{sfn|Njeck|2003a|p=18}}

There are three level tones (high {{IPA|[á]}}, mid {{IPA|[ā]}}, low {{IPA|[à]}}) and three contour tones (low-rising {{IPA|[ǎ]}}, high-low falling {{IPA|[â]}}, and low-falling {{IPA|[ȁ]}}).{{sfn|Njeck|2003a|p=16}} The mid tone is rare but contrasts with the high and low-falling tones.{{sfn|Njeck|2003a|p=18}}

